-- title:
--   Existence of an archimedean type projector on GL₂(A_F)
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and let $\mathit{tys}$ be an archimedean type family for $F$, that is, data assigning to each infinite place $w$ a number $\mathit{card}\,w$ of types and, for each index $i < \mathit{card}\,w$, a type at $w$ consisting of a dimension $n$ together with a representation of the row-isometry subgroup of $F_w$ on $\mathbb{C}^n$. Then there exists a $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism $Q$ of the space of all functions $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$ with the following three properties. First, $Q\varphi = \varphi$ for every continuous $\varphi$ lying in `archCutSubmodule F tys`, the intersection over the infinite places $w$ of the sums over $i$ of the type submodules attached to $\mathit{tys}.\mathrm{rep}\,w\,i$ along the inclusion `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w`. Second, for every continuous $\varphi$ for which the span $S_\varphi$ of the right translates $x \mapsto \varphi(xk)$, with $k$ ranging over the subgroup generated by the ranges of the maps `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w` over all infinite places $w$, is finite dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$, one has $Q\varphi \in \mathrm{archCutSubmodule}\,F\,\mathit{tys} \sqcap S_\varphi$. Third, for every continuous $y$ in `archCutSubmodule F tys`, every function $f$ and every archimedean type family $\mathit{tys}'$ such that $f$ is a factorisable test function (a product $g \mapsto f_\infty(g_\infty) f_{\mathrm{fin}}(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$ of a compactly supported function smooth in the matrix entries at the infinite places with a compactly supported locally constant function on $GL_2$ of the finite adeles) and $f$ is bi-finite of type $\mathit{tys}'$ (meaning $x \mapsto f(x^{-1})$ lies in `archCutSubmodule F tys'` and $f$ lies in `archDualCutSubmodule F tys'`), there exists a factorisable test function $f'$ that is bi-finite of type $\mathit{tys}$ and satisfies $Q(y * f) = y * f'$, where $(y * f)(g) = \int y(gx) f(x)\,dx$ against the adelic Haar measure on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$.
--
--   This is the existence of the projector onto the part of the continuous $K_\infty^1$-finite functions on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ cut out by a prescribed family of archimedean types, together with the compatibility of that projector with right convolution by factorisable bi-finite test functions. It is used in the analysis of cuspidal constituents, in particular in the bounds for infima of cuspidal subrepresentations intersected with invariants, with level-invariant functions, and in the dichotomy for principal cuspidal constituents.
